## 1. Scope

Requirements for a resource that holds restricted data, for the provider and for its researchers.
Personal data is out of scope, and it needs a resource approved for personal data. Keywords and
conformance steps are in the [RFC conventions](/rfc/conventions/).

## 2. Terms

| Term | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| Restricted data | Data that a licence or a data use agreement limits to named, approved people. It is not personal data. |
| Personal data | Data that can identify a person, directly or by linking. Pseudonymised data is personal data. |
| Approval | The permission from a data owner for one person to use one dataset. |
| Shared copy | One read-only copy of a dataset for a group of approved people. |

## 3. Before you bring data

1. If the data can identify a person, use a resource approved for personal data. If you are not
   sure, ask your data protection officer.
2. If the contract asks for more than section 7 covers, ask the provider to agree terms with the
   data owner.
3. Send your answers to the provider with your access request.

## 4. Requirements, level 1: private copies

| ID | Requirement |
| --- | --- |
| RD1 | The provider MUST give each person a personal account linked to an institutional identity, and MUST NOT permit shared logins. |
| RD2 | The provider MUST let a researcher keep a directory that no other user can read or list, with no default ACLs. |
| RD3 | The provider MUST let a researcher encrypt data at rest with a key that the researcher holds. |
| RD4 | The provider MUST give each job temporary storage that no other job can read, and wipe it when the job ends. |
| RD5 | The provider MUST delete restricted data when a project ends or an account expires, and MUST NOT give it to another user. |
| RD6 | The provider MUST state how long it keeps logs, backups and snapshots. |
| RD7 | The provider MUST bind its administrators to confidentiality. |
| RD8 | The provider MUST tell the affected researchers about an exposure within 72 hours. |
| RD9 | The provider SHOULD offer exclusive nodes, allow outbound internet only through an allowlist, and log privileged administrator actions. |
| RD10 | The provider MUST put RD11 to RD16 in its terms of service. |
| RD11 | The researcher MUST hold their own approval for each dataset, and register the dataset, purpose, path and end date with the provider. |
| RD12 | The researcher MUST keep restricted data encrypted in their private directory, and decrypt it only inside a job (RD2 to RD4). |
| RD13 | The researcher MUST NOT try to identify anyone in the data, and MUST publish only aggregate results. |
| RD14 | The researcher MUST NOT send the data, or extracts from it, to a hosted AI service. A model on the resource is permitted. |
| RD15 | The researcher MUST treat model weights trained on the data as restricted, unless the data owner states otherwise. |
| RD16 | The researcher MUST delete their copy when the project ends or the approval stops. |

## 5. Requirements, level 2: shared copies

Level 2 includes level 1.

| ID | Requirement |
| --- | --- |
| RD17 | The provider MUST NOT make a shared copy before the data owner confirms in writing that it fits the agreement. |
| RD18 | The provider MUST make the shared copy read-only, and readable only by the approved people for that dataset. |
| RD19 | The provider MUST check each approval before it adds a person, and remove the person when the approval stops. |
| RD20 | The provider MUST record each change to the group of approved people. |

## 6. Example implementations (informative)

| ID | Example |
| --- | --- |
| RD1 | WAYF, eduGAIN, LDAP |
| RD2 | POSIX modes, a `getfacl` check |
| RD3 | gocryptfs, age |
| RD4 | Slurm tmpfs job container |
| RD9 | A scheduler flag, a proxy, auditd |
| RD18 to RD20 | FreeIPA, Keycloak |

## 7. Clause map (informative)

| Clause in a data use agreement | Requirements |
| --- | --- |
| Do not share access | RD1, RD2, RD5, RD18 |
| Keep the data secure | RD2 to RD9, RD12 |
| Do not give the data to third parties or online services | RD9, RD14 |
| Do not try to identify anyone | RD13 |
| Report incidents | RD8 |
| Delete the data at the end | RD5, RD16 |

## 8. Rationale (informative)

A data use agreement binds each approved person, not a team. File permissions do not keep out
administrators, backups or other jobs on a node. The requirements therefore also protect the
data, the jobs and the results, after the Five Safes framework of the UK Office for National
Statistics.

## 9. Open questions

1. Does root access by an administrator count as sharing access?
2. Can every provider supply decryption inside a job?
3. Is 72 hours the correct limit for RD8?
